💿 What is a Stack?

A stack is a linear data structure that works on the LIFO  principle:

Last In, First Out
Just like a CD rack, where the last CD you place on top is the first one you take out.

we can also say FILO - First In, Last Out

🔼 push = Add a CD
You push a CD onto the rack — this means you're adding an item to the top of the stack.
Time Complexity: O(1)

🔽 pop = Remove the top CD
You pop a CD from the rack — this means you're removing the item from the top of the stack.
Time Complexity: O(1)

👀 peek = See the top CD
You peek to see what's on top of the stack without removing it
Time Complexity: O(1)


